use "emit_c.a0"

# This file is the source (see the header of compiler/emit_wasm.a0).

# A0 port of the instruction-list post-processing `Code.finish` of src/wasm.ts (DESIGN.md 7a): the
# function body arrives as a list of instructions with SYMBOLIC local indices; `wfzfin` stackifies
# a set and the one get that reads its value when the code between them is balanced (see pass 2),
# turns other set/get pairs into tees, drops dead stores, renumbers the non-parameter locals so that
# ones with disjoint live ranges (widened across loops) share an index, and serializes the list.
# The result is byte-identical to the TypeScript (compiler/wasm_code.a0 is checked against `finish`
# on random lists and on every function body of the test programs).
#
# Input: the table `ins` (u32x128x352: 22528 instructions of 2 words; instruction k is word 2k =
# kind, word 2k+1 = v), the instruction count n and the parameter count np (locals below np are
# never renumbered or removed). The kinds, and the bytes each serializes to (uleb/sleb are the
# LEB128 forms of src/wasm.ts, sleb of the int32 whose bit pattern is v):
#    0 NOP nothing           1 OP v the byte v&255      2 CONST v 0x41 sleb(v)
#    3 LGET v 0x20 uleb(v)   4 LSET v 0x21 uleb(v)      5 LTEE v 0x22 uleb(v)   (v renumbered below np)
#    6 CALL v: one marker word v (>= 256)               7 POOL v: one marker word 2^31 + v
#    8 LOOP 0x03 0x40        9 LOOPEND 0x0b             10 LOAD v 0x28 2 uleb(v)  11 STORE v 0x36 2 uleb(v)
#   12 BRIF v 0x0d uleb(v)  13 BR v 0x0c uleb(v)        14 BLOCK v 0x02 v&255     15 IF v 0x04 v&255
#   16 MEMCOPY 0xfc 0x0a 0 0  17 MEMFILL 0xfc 0x0b 0    18 SIMD v 0xfd uleb(v)
#   19 VSTORE v 0xfd 0x0b 2 uleb(v) (v128.store at offset v)
#   20 VCONSTIDX 0xfd 0x0c then the lanes 0 1 2 3 (u32, little endian)
#   21 VCONSTSPLAT v 0xfd 0x0c then v (little endian) four times
#   22 GGET v 0x23 v&255    23 GSET v 0x24 v&255
#   24 VEXTRACT v 0xfd 0x1b v&255 (i32x4.extract_lane)   25 VREPLACE v 0xfd 0x1c v&255 (replace_lane)
#   26 VCONST v 0xfd 0x0c then v (little endian): lane 0 of a v128.const whose lanes 1..3 follow
#   27 WORD v v (little endian): a lane of the v128.const before it
# A local id below 2^20 (VBASE) is an i32 local (id < 8192 when not a parameter), an id VBASE + k
# (k < 128) a v128 local; the v128 locals are placed after the i32 ones. A local id outside these
# ranges, more than 22528 instructions, or more than 65533 output words is the failure value.
# Loops (kinds 8, 9) are balanced and nested; blocks and ifs are not loops.
#
# Result (wfzfin): the code table (u32x128x512). Words 0 .. nwords-1 are the body, one word per
# byte plus a marker word for each CALL/POOL; the last three words are the header: word 65533 =
# nwords, the number of words written (4294967295 on failure, then the other two are 0), word
# 65534 = nlocals (the i32 locals above the np parameters) and word 65535 = nvlocals (the v128
# locals), i.e. `locals` and `vlocals` of `Code.finish`. (A record with the table would pass
# the 2^21 bit limit of a value, so the three scalars live in the table: the body holds at most
# 65533 words.)
#
# Method. Every pass is a fold over the instructions whose state is a table (u32x128x512 = 65536
# words, element i at page i>>7, word i&127), updated in place; tables read by a pass are fold
# extras (borrowed, never copied), and a write is a one-trip fold of a tiny body (`wfzp1`, ...).
# 1. wfzcnt: gets and sets per local (a LTEE counts as a set) over the original list.
# 2. wfzfw, wfzver, wfzout: stackify (the three folds of pass 2 and the effect tables before them):
#    a set whose one read is balanced code away stays on the operand stack with that read removed;
#    a set directly followed by its read becomes a tee; a dead set becomes OP 0x1a, a dead tee
#    vanishes. A removed instruction is kind 0; positions stay the original indices.
# 3. wfzrng: per local its first and last access and the top-level (outermost) loop around each;
#    per top-level loop its start and end. Since loops nest, repeated widening against all loops
#    is the hull with the outermost loop around the first access (start) and last access (end).
# 4. wfzalc: the locals in order of first access (the TypeScript stable sort by widened start gives
#    the same order) take the first slot whose end is below the widened start; i32 and v128 locals
#    have separate slot sets; the slot is kept per local.
# 5. wfzoff, wfzcode: the offset of every instruction (running sum of its length), then its
#    bytes, written one by one (wfzbyte).
# The tables start as `wfzz` (all zero) and are laid out as follows (word indices):
#   count table  : gets of local c at c, sets at 8320 + c (c: i32 id, or 8192 + k for VBASE + k),
#                  16640: set to 1 when a local id is out of range, 16641 scratch
#   range table  : 0 loop depth, 1 top-level loop count, 8 9 16..19 scratch, 128 + 4c: first
#                  access + 1, its top-level loop, last access, its top-level loop,
#                  33408 + L: start and 44928 + L: end of top-level loop L
#   slot table   : c: slot of local c, 8320 + s: end of i32 slot s, 16512 + s: end of v128 slot
#                  s, 16640 and 16641: slots used (i32, v128), 16650 and 16651 scratch
#   offset table : word i is the offset of instruction i (n + 1 words)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tables

# word p1 of the table p0
fn wfzg u32x128x512 u32 -> u32
a shr p1 7
b get p0 a
c and p1 127
d get b c
ret d
end
# word p1 of the input list
fn wfzgi u32x128x352 u32 -> u32
a shr p1 7
b get p0 a
c and p1 127
d get b c
ret d
end
# the state with word p2 set to p3 (a fold of one trip: p1 is the trip)
fn wfzp1 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shr p2 7
b get p0 a
c and p2 127
d set b c p3
e set p0 a d
ret e
end
# the state with the words p2 and p2 + 1 (same page) set to p3 and p4
fn wfzp2 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shr p2 7
b get p0 a
c and p2 127
d set b c p3
e add c 1
f set d e p4
g set p0 a f
ret g
end
# the state with the words p2 .. p2 + 3 (p2 a multiple of 4) set to p3 .. p6
fn wfzp4 u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shr p2 7
b get p0 a
c and p2 127
d set b c p3
e add c 1
f set d e p4
g add c 2
h set f g p5
i add c 3
j set h i p6
k set p0 a j
ret k
end
# the zero table
fn wfzz -> u32x128x512
a call zpage
b arr a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a
ret b
end
# the zero input list
fn wfzzi -> u32x128x352
a call zpage
b arr a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a a
ret b
end
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local ids

# 1 for a local access kind (3 get, 4 set, 5 tee)
fn wfzisl u32 -> bool
a sub p0 3
b lt a 3
ret b
end
# the compact index of local id p0: i32 ids below 8192 as they are, VBASE + k (k < 128) as 8192 + k,
# 0 for an id out of range
fn wfzcidx u32 -> u32
a lt p0 8192
b sub p0 1048576
c lt b 128
d add b 8192
e select c d 0
f select a p0 e
ret f
end
# is local id p0 in range
fn wfzvok u32 -> bool
a lt p0 8192
b sub p0 1048576
c lt b 128
d or a c
ret d
end
# the final index of local id p0 (slot table p0, parameters p1, i32 locals p2): parameters stay,
# an i32 local is np + slot, a v128 local np + nl + slot
fn wfzmap u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzcidx p3
b shr a 7
c and a 127
d get p0 b
e get d c
f lt p3 8192
g lt p3 p1
h add p1 e
i add p1 p2
j add i e
k select f h j
l select g p3 k
ret l
end
# the operand of an instruction after renumbering: the final index for a local access (kind p3,
# value p4), else p4
fn wfzuse u32x128x512 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzisl p3
b call wfzmap p0 p1 p2 p4
c select a b p4
ret c
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bytes

# bytes of the uleb128 form of p0 (1..5)
fn wfzul u32 -> u32
a ge p0 128
b ge p0 16384
c ge p0 2097152
d ge p0 268435456
e select a 1 0
f select b 1 0
g select c 1 0
h select d 1 0
i add e f
j add i g
k add j h
l add k 1
ret l
end
# bytes of the sleb128 form of the int32 with the bit pattern p0 (1..5)
fn wfzsl u32 -> u32
a add p0 64
b add p0 8192
c add p0 1048576
d add p0 134217728
e ge a 128
f ge b 16384
g ge c 2097152
h ge d 268435456
i select e 1 0
j select f 1 0
k select g 1 0
l select h 1 0
m add i j
n add m k
o add n l
p add o 1
ret p
end
# byte p1 of the uleb128 form of p0
fn wfzuleb u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzul p0
b add p1 1
c lt b a
d mul p1 7
e shr p0 d
f and e 127
g or f 128
h select c g f
ret h
end
# byte p1 of the sleb128 form of the int32 with the bit pattern p0
fn wfzsleb u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzsl p0
b add p1 1
c lt b a
d mul p1 7
e shr p0 d
f shr p0 31
g eq f 1
h gt d 0
i and g h
j sub 32 d
k shl 4294967295 j
l select i k 0
m or e l
n and m 127
o or n 128
p select c o n
ret p
end
# length of the fixed prefix of kind p0
fn wfzplen u32 -> u32
a mov 0
b eq p0 2
c select b 1 a
d eq p0 3
e select d 1 c
f eq p0 4
g select f 1 e
h eq p0 5
i select h 1 g
j eq p0 8
k select j 2 i
l eq p0 9
m select l 1 k
n eq p0 10
o select n 2 m
p eq p0 11
q select p 2 o
r eq p0 12
s select r 1 q
t eq p0 13
u select t 1 s
v eq p0 14
w select v 1 u
x eq p0 15
y select x 1 w
z eq p0 16
aa select z 4 y
ab eq p0 17
ac select ab 3 aa
ad eq p0 18
ae select ad 1 ac
af eq p0 19
ag select af 4 ae
ah eq p0 20
ai select ah 2 ag
aj eq p0 21
ak select aj 2 ai
al eq p0 22
am select al 1 ak
an eq p0 23
ao select an 1 am
b0 eq p0 19
b1 select b0 3 ao
b2 eq p0 24
b3 select b2 2 b1
b4 eq p0 25
b5 select b4 2 b3
b6 eq p0 26
b7 select b6 2 b5
ret b7
end
# the fixed prefix bytes of kind p0, packed little endian
fn wfzpack u32 -> u32
a mov 0
b eq p0 2
c select b 65 a
d eq p0 3
e select d 32 c
f eq p0 4
g select f 33 e
h eq p0 5
i select h 34 g
j eq p0 8
k select j 16387 i
l eq p0 9
m select l 11 k
n eq p0 10
o select n 552 m
p eq p0 11
q select p 566 o
r eq p0 12
s select r 13 q
t eq p0 13
u select t 12 s
v eq p0 14
w select v 2 u
x eq p0 15
y select x 4 w
z eq p0 16
aa select z 2812 y
ab eq p0 17
ac select ab 3068 aa
ad eq p0 18
ae select ad 253 ac
af eq p0 19
ag select af 134141 ae
ah eq p0 20
ai select ah 3325 ag
aj eq p0 21
ak select aj 3325 ai
al eq p0 22
am select al 35 ak
an eq p0 23
ao select an 36 am
b0 eq p0 24
b1 select b0 7165 ao
b2 eq p0 25
b3 select b2 7421 b1
b4 eq p0 26
b5 select b4 3325 b3
ret b5
end
# length of the variable part of kind p0 whose operand is p1
fn wfzvlen u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzul p1
b call wfzsl p1
c mov 0
d eq p0 1
e select d 1 c
f eq p0 2
g select f b e
h eq p0 3
i select h a g
j eq p0 4
k select j a i
l eq p0 5
m select l a k
n eq p0 6
o select n 1 m
p eq p0 7
q select p 1 o
r eq p0 10
s select r a q
t eq p0 11
u select t a s
v eq p0 12
w select v a u
x eq p0 13
y select x a w
z eq p0 14
aa select z 1 y
ab eq p0 15
ac select ab 1 aa
ad eq p0 18
ae select ad a ac
af eq p0 20
ag select af 16 ae
ah eq p0 21
ai select ah 16 ag
aj eq p0 22
ak select aj 1 ai
al eq p0 23
am select al 1 ak
b0 eq p0 19
b1 select b0 a am
b2 eq p0 24
b3 eq p0 25
b4 or b2 b3
b5 select b4 1 b1
b6 eq p0 26
b7 eq p0 27
b8 or b6 b7
b9 select b8 4 b5
ret b9
end
# words of the instruction of kind p0 with operand p1 (a local access: its final index)
fn wfzlen u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzplen p0
b call wfzvlen p0 p1
c add a b
ret c
end
# the variable byte p2 of kind p0 with operand p1 (the index counts from the end of the prefix)
fn wfzvar u32 u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzuleb p1 p2
b call wfzsleb p1 p2
c and p1 255
d and p2 3
e mul d 8
f shr p1 e
g and f 255
h eq d 0
i shr p2 2
j select h i 0
k add p1 2147483648
l mov 0
m eq p0 1
n select m c l
o eq p0 2
p select o b n
q eq p0 3
r select q a p
s eq p0 4
t select s a r
u eq p0 5
v select u a t
w eq p0 6
x select w p1 v
y eq p0 7
z select y k x
aa eq p0 10
ab select aa a z
ac eq p0 11
ad select ac a ab
ae eq p0 12
af select ae a ad
ag eq p0 13
ah select ag a af
ai eq p0 14
aj select ai c ah
ak eq p0 15
al select ak c aj
am eq p0 18
an select am a al
ao eq p0 20
ap select ao j an
aq eq p0 21
ar select aq g ap
as eq p0 22
au select as c ar
av eq p0 23
aw select av c au
b0 eq p0 19
b1 select b0 a aw
b2 eq p0 24
b3 eq p0 25
b4 or b2 b3
b5 select b4 c b1
b6 mul p2 8
b7 shr p1 b6
b8 and b7 255
b9 eq p0 26
c0 eq p0 27
c1 or b9 c0
c2 select c1 b8 b5
ret c2
end
# word p2 of the instruction of kind p0 with operand p1: a byte, or a marker for a call or a pool address
fn wfzbyte u32 u32 u32 -> u32
a call wfzplen p0
b call wfzpack p0
c lt p2 a
d mul p2 8
e shr b d
f and e 255
g sub p2 a
h call wfzvar p0 p1 g
i select c f h
ret i
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pass 1: counts. State: the count table; trip i: instruction i of p2 (n = p4, np = p3).

# a get of a local adds one to its gets, a set or tee to its sets
fn wfzcnt u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x352 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shl p1 1
b call wfzgi p2 a
c add a 1
d call wfzgi p2 c
e call wfzisl b
f ge d p3
g lt p1 p4
h and e f
i and h g
j call wfzcidx d
k call wfzvok d
l eq b 3
m add j 8320
n select l j m
o and i k
p select o 1 0
q shr n 7
r and n 127
s get p0 q
t get s r
u add t p
v eq k false
w and i v
x select w 16640 16641
y shr n 7
z get p0 y
aa and n 127
ab set z aa u
ac set p0 y ab
ad shr x 7
ae get ac ad
af and x 127
ag set ae af 1
ah set ac ad ag
ret ah
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pass 2: stackify (src/wasm.ts `stackify`). Three folds over the list and one table of effects:
# the forward pass wfzfw (state W, see below) records the depth before every instruction and the
# partner get of every set that qualifies; the verification wfzver (state F) takes the pairs in
# order of their sets, checking the span between with wfzspan; the output wfzout (state O, two
# words per instruction) writes the stackified list. A removed instruction is kind 0.
#
# The stack effect of an instruction of kind p0 and value p1 (src/wasm.ts `effectOf` and
# `runEffect`): net is its change of depth, low the lowest depth it reaches relative to its start
# (two's complement: 4294967295 is -1). An instruction with no known effect (kind 0, 6, 8, 9, 12..15,
# a SIMD (18) other than a splat or a lane-wise operation, or an OP byte outside the table) is a barrier.

# the single-byte op p0 has a known stack effect: drop 0x1a, select 0x1b, eqz 0x45, a comparison
# 0x46..0x4f, a unary op 0x67..0x69 or a binary op 0x6a..0x78
fn wfzopok u32 -> bool
a eq p0 26
b eq p0 27
c eq p0 69
d ge p0 70
e le p0 79
f and d e
g ge p0 103
h le p0 120
i and g h
j or a b
k or j c
l or k f
m or l i
ret m
end
# the net depth change of the single-byte op p0
fn wfzopnet u32 -> u32
a eq p0 26
b eq p0 27
c ge p0 70
d le p0 79
e and c d
f ge p0 106
g le p0 120
h and f g
i select h 4294967295 0
j select e 4294967295 i
k select b 4294967294 j
l select a 4294967295 k
ret l
end
# the lowest depth the single-byte op p0 reaches relative to its start
fn wfzoplow u32 -> u32
a eq p0 26
b eq p0 27
c eq p0 69
d ge p0 70
e le p0 79
f and d e
g ge p0 103
h le p0 105
i and g h
j ge p0 106
k le p0 120
l and j k
m select l 4294967294 0
n select f 4294967294 m
o select b 4294967293 n
p select a 4294967295 o
q select i 4294967295 p
r select c 4294967295 q
ret r
end
# the simd128 opcode p0 (kind 18) is a lane-wise i32x4 operation of two operands (src/wasm.ts
# `SLP_OPS`: and or xor shl shr_u add sub mul)
fn wfzvbin u32 -> bool
a eq p0 78
b eq p0 80
c eq p0 81
d eq p0 171
e eq p0 173
f eq p0 174
g eq p0 177
h eq p0 181
i or a b
j or i c
k or j d
l or k e
m or l f
n or m g
o or n h
ret o
end
# 1 when an instruction of kind p0 and value p1 is a barrier (has no known stack effect): simd128
# runs have known effects (kinds 19..21, 24..27, and a splat or a lane-wise operation of kind 18)
fn wfzbar u32 u32 -> bool
a eq p0 1
b call wfzopok p1
c eq p0 2
d eq p0 3
e eq p0 4
f eq p0 5
g eq p0 7
h eq p0 10
i eq p0 11
j eq p0 16
k eq p0 17
l eq p0 22
m eq p0 23
n or c d
o or n e
p or o f
q or p g
r or q h
s or r i
t or s j
u or t k
v or u l
w or v m
b0 eq p0 18
b1 eq p1 17
b2 call wfzvbin p1
b3 or b1 b2
b4 and b0 b3
b5 ge p0 19
b6 le p0 21
b7 and b5 b6
b8 ge p0 24
b9 le p0 27
c0 and b8 b9
c1 or w b4
c2 or c1 b7
c3 or c2 c0
x select a b c3
y eq x false
ret y
end
# the net depth change of an instruction of kind p0 and value p1
fn wfznet u32 u32 -> u32
a eq p0 2
b eq p0 3
c eq p0 7
d eq p0 22
e or a b
f or e c
g or f d
h eq p0 4
i eq p0 23
j or h i
k eq p0 11
l eq p0 16
m eq p0 17
n or l m
o call wfzopnet p1
p select g 1 0
q select j 4294967295 p
r select k 4294967294 q
s select n 4294967293 r
t eq p0 1
u select t o s
b0 eq p0 18
b1 call wfzvbin p1
b2 select b1 4294967295 0
b3 select b0 b2 u
b4 eq p0 19
b5 select b4 4294967294 b3
b6 eq p0 20
b7 eq p0 21
b8 eq p0 26
b9 or b6 b7
c0 or b9 b8
c1 select c0 1 b5
c2 eq p0 25
c3 select c2 4294967295 c1
ret c3
end
# the lowest depth an instruction of kind p0 and value p1 reaches relative to its start
fn wfzlow u32 u32 -> u32
a eq p0 2
b eq p0 3
c eq p0 7
