# Forward pass, one trip per instruction k = p1 of the list p2 (np = p3). State W, all words of
# one u32x128x512 table: word k is the depth before instruction k, counted from the start of its
# run (the code between barriers) and biased by 2^20 (the depth is never below 2^20 - 22528);
# word 22528 + k is 1 + the position of the get that pairs with the set at k, 0 when there is no
# pair (set at k and get of the same local, one get in the set's range, the set's run the get's run,
# and no earlier get of the local in the outermost loop before the set); words 45056 + c (c the
# compact index of a local, wfzcidx) hold 2(p + 1) + loopOK of the open range of c (p the set's
# position, 0 when no range is open), words 53376 + c hold the last get of c plus 1 at bits 17..31,
# the run of the open range at bits 2..16 and the gets the range has read at bits 0..1 (0, 1, or 2
# for more or a get in another run); words 61696..61699 hold the depth, the run, the loop depth and
# the loop start. Word 65530 absorbs the writes that do not apply.
fn wfzfw u32x128x512 u32 u32x128x352 u32 -> u32x128x512
a shl p1 1
b call wfzgi p2 a
c add a 1
d call wfzgi p2 c
